<Project>
  <!--
    THE ONE VERSION NUMBER for Masterplan (M14) and the MasterplanXP Migration Tool.

    Both projects import this file (Masterplan141\Masterplan.csproj and
    MigrationTool\MasterplanXP.MigrationTool\MasterplanXP.MigrationTool.csproj), so they always carry
    the same version, and Release\Build-Release.ps1 reads it from here for the zip names.
    Never put <Version>, <AssemblyVersion> or <FileVersion> in either .csproj again: change it HERE.

    WHEN TO BUMP (format 14.1.<format>.<build>), once per commit that changes either program
    (code, XAML, project files), not once per edit. Commits that only change documentation do not bump.
      - Any change to M14 or to the migration tool:       4th number   14.1.0.4 -> 14.1.0.5
      - File format change (a new [Key] in DtoModels.cs,  3rd number,  14.1.0.9 -> 14.1.1.0
        in either copy):                                  4th resets
      - M14.2 / MPX milestones: 1st / 2nd number, decided by the project owner.

    Why one number: every release zip ships both programs together, and the tool writes the
    .mpxlib / .mpxplan files that M14 reads, so the two must always be built from the same state.
    The migration tool shows this version in its window title and in migration_log.txt.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Version>14.1.1.4</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>14.1.1.4</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>14.1.1.4</FileVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
